        <mxCell id="-DPXh-h7QqhF4jSscgDO-75" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Islanded microgrid – diesel + PV + battery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No utility connection: the largest genset (G1, 1.0 MVA) is the reference (slack) machine,&lt;br&gt;G2 (0.8 MVA) runs at a fixed 0.25 MW.&lt;br&gt;An 11 kV network supplies a village, a water plant with a 200 kW borehole pump and a&lt;br&gt;PV + battery site (600 kWp, 250 kW / 1 MWh charging).&lt;br&gt;Short-circuit current comes only from the gensets (X&quot;d = 0.13 pu) and the PV inverters (k = 1.2).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Try:&lt;/b&gt; Load Flow – genset loading and voltage profile; Short Circuit IEC 60909 – low fault&lt;br&gt;levels typical of island grids (check protection sensitivity); start the pump with Motor Starting." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=8;fontSize=12;fillColor=#e8f5e9;strokeColor=#81c784;" vertex="1" parent="-DPXh-h7QqhF4jSscgDO-1">
          <mxGeometry x="520" y="20" width="660" height="173.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
